#: ../../tools/nasa_donki_tools.rst:98 fe2b5ae6a25f43fb99a367b3b63c6faa
msgid ""
"**Description**: Search NASA DONKI for High Speed Stream (HSS) events in "
"the solar wind. HSSs originate from coronal holes on the Sun and can "
"cause minor to moderate geomagnetic storming when they interact with "
"Earth's magnetosphere. They produce recurrent geomagnetic activity "
"patterns (27-day cycle) and are a major source of space weather "
"disturbances during solar minimum. No API key required."
msgstr ""

