#: ../../tools/nasa_donki_tools.rst:131 691ba5dd4eea4241bcae120feaa204ca
msgid ""
"**Description**: Search NASA DONKI for Interplanetary Shock (IPS) events "
"detected at Earth or in the solar wind. Interplanetary shocks are sudden "
"increases in solar wind speed, density, and magnetic field strength, "
"often driven by CMEs or stream interaction regions. They can trigger "
"geomagnetic storms. Returns event time, location, detecting instruments, "
"and linked events. No API key required."
msgstr ""

